{"code": "M11L2V3Q3", "page": 10, "stem_ok": false, "stem_book": "If the general solution of the equation cos²θ = 1/2 is in the form nπ ± K, n ∈ Z, then the value of K/2π is", "figure": null, "type": "numerical", "options_printed": false, "key": "0.125", "derived": "0.125", "verdict": "ok", "correct_answer": "0.125", "integer": false, "in_scope": true, "reason": "", "work": "cos²θ = cos²(π/4) ⇒ θ = nπ ± π/4 ⇒ K/2π = (π/4)/(2π) = 1/8 = 0.125"}
